  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE ROAD TO SUSTAINABILITY IN BAJA CALIFORNIA: PRIORITIZING THREATS AND BUILDINGCAPACITY FOR EFFECTIVE MANAGEMENT, MONITORING, AND CONSERVATION OF THE CALIFORNIA CONDOR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project represents a comprehensive and critical effort to build capacity for the recovery of California condors in the Sierra de San Pedro Mrtir region of Baja California, Mexico and supports the Memorandum of Understanding for the reintroduction of the California condor in Mexico signed by the USFWS and the Mexican Commission of Natural Protected Areas (CONANP) in 2015. Thus, the proposed project will: i) evaluate the main threats to California condors in the San Pedro Martir National Park release.site; ii) build capacity through public engagement, increased monitoring, and strengthening partnerships for effectively managing.threats to California condors in Baja California; iii) monitor condors for lead and trash-related mortalities; iii) conduct public</narrative>
  </description>
